@startuml 08-pkce
!include ../ssh/explainer/diagrams/theme-oriolrius.puml
title PKCE: a one-time proof instead of a client secret
start
:Frontend generates a random **code_verifier**
(43–128 characters);
:Frontend computes
""code_challenge = base64url(sha256(code_verifier))"";
:Authorization request sends the **code_challenge**
(not the verifier)
""GET /authorize?code_challenge=…&code_challenge_method=S256"";
:Token request sends the **code_verifier**
""POST /token  code=…  code_verifier=…"";
if (Keycloak: sha256(code_verifier) = stored code_challenge?) then (match)
  :Issue tokens to this client; <<#E7F6F0>>
else (no match)
  :Reject; <<#FDECEC>>
endif
stop
@enduml
